course: french
lesson: 12
title: Telling the time
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: To ask the time in French you say Quelle heure est-il ?, and the answer is Il est trois heures, word for word "it is three hours", which simply means three o'clock.
explain: Heure is a feminine word, so one o'clock is une heure, and from two o'clock on it takes an s: deux heures.
explain: Quarter past is et quart and half past is et demie; for times before the hour you take away from the next hour with moins: cinq heures moins le quart is quarter to five.
explain: Picture a Paris station: the board says 14h30, because French timetables use the 24-hour clock; take 12 away and you know it is half past two in the afternoon.
explain: Noon and midnight have their own words, midi and minuit, and the day is split into le matin, l'après-midi and le soir.
fact: Quelle heure est-il ? means "What time is it?"; Il est trois heures means "It's three o'clock".
fact: heure is feminine: Il est une heure (one o'clock) has no s; Il est deux heures (two o'clock) has an s.
fact: French timetables, cinemas and shops use the 24-hour clock written with h: 14h30 is quatorze heures trente, half past two in the afternoon.
fact: et quart means quarter past and et demie means half past: deux heures et quart, deux heures et demie; after heures, half is written demie, with an e.
fact: moins means minus: cinq heures moins le quart is quarter to five, cinq heures moins dix is ten to five.
fact: midi means noon and minuit means midnight; le Midi is also a name for the south of France.
fact: à + a time means "at": Le cours commence à neuf heures (the lesson starts at nine); neuf heures sounds like "nuh-VUR".
fact: le matin is the morning, l'après-midi (after-midday) is the afternoon and le soir is the evening, from about 6 pm.
fact: Debout ! ("duh-BOO") means "Get up!"; word for word it means standing.
fact: À quelle heure ? means "At what time?"; in France dinner is often late, around 19h30 or 20h.
fact: With a clock face people often say trois heures moins vingt (twenty to three); with a digital clock deux heures quarante (2:40) is fine too.
fact: Slang here: "like" at the end (Yorkshire) adds a shrug; "wee" (Northern Ireland) means small; "sure" (Ireland) starts a sentence; "y'all" (Texas) means you all; "ah'm no" (Scotland) means I'm not; "arvo" (Australia) means afternoon; "my lover" (Bath) means dear.
exercise: Noah asks the time. What does Il est trois heures mean? | It's three o'clock | It's three hours long | It's been three hours | It's at three hours
exercise: How do you ask "What time is it?" | Quelle heure est-il ? | Quel temps fait-il ? | Quelle heure il a ? | Combien d'heures ?
exercise: Mia says "Il est un heure". What is right? | Il est une heure. | Il est une heures. | Il est un heures. | Il est uns heure.
exercise: What time is 14h30? | half past two in the afternoon | half past four | fourteen minutes past three | half past two at night
exercise: How do you write "half past two" in French? | deux heures et demie | deux heures et demi | deux heure et demie | deux heures et moitié
exercise: What does et quart mean after a time? | quarter past | quarter to | half past | four o'clock
exercise: What time is cinq heures moins le quart? | quarter to five | quarter past five | quarter to four | five fifteen
exercise: What is midi? | 12 noon | midnight | a skirt | the middle of the night
exercise: What is minuit? | midnight | noon | one minute | a small night
exercise: The teacher says the lesson starts à neuf heures. When should Jacob come? | at nine o'clock | at about nine minutes past | after nine hours | at ten to nine
exercise: How does neuf heures sound? | "nuh-VUR" | "nuhf-UR" | "nuh-UR" | "noof-HURS"
exercise: Which word is the afternoon? | l'après-midi | le soir | le matin | la nuit
exercise: What does Debout ! mean when Mum shouts it at seven? | Get up! | Do a boot! | Go to bed! | Shut the door!
exercise: How do you ask "At what time is dinner?" | À quelle heure est le dîner ? | Quelle heure le dîner ? | Quelle heure est-il le dîner ? | Le dîner est quelle ?
exercise: What is trois heures moins vingt? | twenty to three | twenty past three | three twenty | twenty to two
exercise: Freya's host says dinner is à vingt heures. What time is that? | 8 pm | 10 pm | 2 pm | 12 pm
test: Noah asks, "Three hours of what?" What's the truth about Il est trois heures? | heures here means o'clock: it is three o'clock | It means the class has been on for three hours | It means you must wait three hours | It means it is three in the morning only
test: Mia shrugs, "Wee word, wee mistake." ("Wee" means small.) Why does une heure need une? | heure is a feminine word | heure is a word for girls only | une is used for times before noon | une means "o'clock"
test: Oliver says, "There's no fourteen o'clock, like." What would happen if he read 14h30 as 4:30? | He would miss his train by two hours | He would be two hours early for nothing | Nothing, 14h30 and 4:30 are the same | He would be half an hour late
test: Ava says "sure that's like half and quarter, grand," then writes "deux heures et demi". What's the mistake? | After heures, half is written demie with an e | Half past is et quart, not et demi | Demi must always go before heures | There is no mistake at all
test: Jake in Dallas says, "Five hours minus something? Y'all are making clocks hard." What is cinq heures moins dix? | ten to five | ten past five | five past ten | ten to four
test: Lily asks, "Is midi like a skirt?" when her penpal says "Il est midi !" What does it mean? | It's 12 noon | It's half past twelve | It's a skirt time | It's midnight
test: Jacob in Glasgow says proudly, "Ah'm no late for once." ("Ah'm no" means I'm not.) When did his class start? | à neuf heures, at nine | at nineteen hours | after nine lessons | nine minutes past
test: Olivia in Melbourne asks, "Arvo's not a thing in French?" ("Arvo" means afternoon.) At 3 pm, what should she say? | l'après-midi | le soir | le matin | la nuit
test: Harvey grumbles, "Does it want me to do a boot?" when his alarm says "Debout !" What does it mean? | Get up! | Put your boots on! | Go back to sleep! | Kick the alarm!
test: Freya's gran says, "That's eight! I'd starve, my lover." ("My lover" means dear.) What's true about dinner in France? | It is often around 19h30 or 20h, later than in many UK homes | It is always at 16h, straight after school | It is at midnight in summer | There is no evening meal in France
test: ★★★ The film starts à quatorze heures quarante-cinq and lasts one hour and a half. When does it end, the clock-face way? | quatre heures et quart | trois heures et quart | quatre heures moins le quart | quatre heures et demie
test: ★★★ It is deux heures moins le quart. Max's bus comes in twenty minutes. What time does it come? | deux heures cinq | deux heures et quart | une heure cinq | deux heures moins cinq
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the grammatical gender of the noun heure? | It is feminine, whence the expression une heure | It is masculine, whence the expression un heure | It possesses no gender whatsoever | It is masculine in the singular and feminine in the plural
exam: Identify the time denoted by the expression cinq heures moins le quart. | A quarter of an hour before five o'clock | A quarter of an hour after five o'clock | Five minutes before four o'clock | Five hours less a quarter of a day
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning the notation 14h30 upon a French timetable. | It denotes half past two in the afternoon, upon the twenty-four-hour system | It denotes half past four in the morning, upon the twelve-hour system | It denotes fourteen minutes past three in the afternoon | It denotes a duration of fourteen hours and thirty minutes
exam: It is given that a lesson is stated to commence à neuf heures. Ascertain the hour of its commencement. | Nine o'clock | Nineteen o'clock | Nine minutes past the hour | Ten minutes to nine
